## Threat model

This target uses `attacker_controls = {{ attacker_controls }}`. A security
issue whose trigger those controls fully determine is in-model; one that also
needs something outside them is kept as a real defect but earns no security
credit.

An extra component is narrow — a post-parse call order, a lifetime or teardown
order, timing, concurrency, environment, or filesystem state that the
application chooses. Its fixed, contract-obeying setup is not one: creating or
reusing a context, selecting a supported mode, and calling the documented entry
point are things it does whatever the input says.

Aim at faults the listed controls reach, but never pre-filter: report what
reproduces and name the extra component. Triage makes that comparison once.
